An intelligence agency has received reports about some threats. The reports consist of numbers in a mysterious method. There is a number 
“N” and another number “R”. Those numbers are studied thoroughly and it is concluded that all digits of the number ‘N’ are summed up and 
this action is performed ‘R’ number of times. The resultant is also a single digit that is yet to be deciphered. The task here is to find
the single-digit sum of the given number ‘N’ by repeating the action ‘R’ number of times.If the value of $R = 0$, print $0$.Inputs & Sample 
Test CaseInput:N = 99 R = 3
Explanation / Calculation:Sum of digits of N: $9 + 9 = 18$Repeat $R$ times: $18 \times 3 = 54$Single-digit reduction of 54: 5 + 4 = 9
Output:9





#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n,r;
    cin>>n>>r;
    if(r==0){
        cout<<0;
        return 0;
    }
    int sum=0;
    while(n!=0){
        int digit=n%10;
        sum+=digit;
        n=n/10;
    }
    sum=sum*r;
    
    //digital root formula
    
    int result= (int)(1+(sum-1)%9);
    cout<<result<<endl;
    
    return 0;
}




